## Building a Recipe Scaler

### Ingredient Structure

```xiom
type Ingredient {
  name: Str;
  amount: Int;
  unit: Str;
}

type Recipe {
  name: Str;
  servings: Int;
  ingredients: Vec[Ingredient];
}
```

### Scaling

```xiom
fn scale_recipe(recipe: &Recipe, desired_servings: Int) -> Vec[Ingredient] {
  let scale = desired_servings / recipe.servings;
  let remainder = desired_servings % recipe.servings;

  let mut scaled: Vec[Ingredient] = Vec[Ingredient].new();
  let mut i = 0;
  while i < recipe.ingredients.len() {
    let ing = recipe.ingredients.get(i).unwrap();
    let new_amount = ing.amount * scale;
    scaled.push(Ingredient{
      name: ing.name.clone(),
      amount: new_amount,
      unit: ing.unit.clone()
    });
    i += 1;
  };
  scaled
}
```

### Handling Fractional Amounts

```xiom
fn format_amount(whole: Int, fraction: Int, denominator: Int) -> Str {
  let mut result = "";
  if whole > 0 {
    result = int_to_str(whole);
  };
  if fraction > 0 {
    if whole > 0 {
      result = string.str_concat(result, " and ");
    };
    result = string.str_concat(result, int_to_str(fraction));
    result = string.str_concat(result, "/");
    result = string.str_concat(result, int_to_str(denominator));
  };
  if whole == 0 && fraction == 0 {
    result = "0";
  };
  result
}
```

### Example

Original (24 cookies):
- 2 cups flour
- 1 cup sugar
- 2 eggs

Scaled to 60 cookies (×2.5):
- 5 cups flour (2 × 2.5)
- 2 and 1/2 cups sugar (1 × 2.5)
- 5 eggs (2 × 2.5)

### Halving a Recipe

```xiom
fn halve_recipe(recipe: &Recipe) -> Vec[Ingredient] {
  let mut halved: Vec[Ingredient] = Vec[Ingredient].new();
  let mut i = 0;
  while i < recipe.ingredients.len() {
    let ing = recipe.ingredients.get(i).unwrap();
    halved.push(Ingredient{
      name: ing.name.clone(),
      amount: ing.amount / 2,
      unit: ing.unit.clone()
    });
    i += 1;
  };
  halved
}
```

